{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01VfEoGBY42u9C9S7f1J7L3c","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"liquid lithium self-diffusion \"cm2/s\" experimental 470 K 6.9e-5 OR \"D0\" activation energy NMR Murday Cotts 1968 values\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"link.springer.com\",\"url\":\"https://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/BF00883553\"},{\"title\":\"self diffusion coefficient study of liquid lithium\",\"url\":\"https://scholar.xjtu.edu.cn/en/publications/self-diffusion-coefficient-study-of-liquid-lithium/\"},{\"title\":\"Self-diffusion coefficients of ionic liquids measured by multinuclear benchtop NMR\",\"url\":\"https://magritek.com/?p=21016\"},{\"title\":\"s00231 011 0874 9\",\"url\":\"https://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/s00231-011-0874-9\"},{\"title\":\"Issue 0, 1977\",\"url\":\"https://pubs.rsc.org/en/Content/ArticleLanding/1977/F1/F19777301731\"},{\"title\":\"Self-diffusion and isotopic effects in liquid lithium\",\"url\":\"https://scilit.com/publications/a87ad4db2680c466d4fc33f00ce090a5\"},{\"title\":\"subject:Self diffusion coefficients\",\"url\":\"https://fitforthem.unipa.it/subject:Self-diffusion coefficients\"},{\"title\":\"dspace.bits-pilani.ac.in\",\"url\":\"https://dspace.bits-pilani.ac.in/items/8ed4634f-035a-4192-822c-4f03ec20d341/full\"},{\"title\":\"Quasielastic neutron scattering and diffusion in liquid lithium and lithium–hydrogen melt\",\"url\":\"https://hal-insu.archives-ouvertes.fr/insu-00332070\"},{\"title\":\"8ed4634f 035a 4192 822c 4f03ec20d341\",\"url\":\"https://dspace.bits-pilani.ac.in/items/8ed4634f-035a-4192-822c-4f03ec20d341\"}]\n\nThe search did not turn up the Murday & Cotts numerical values (D0, activation energy, or D at 470 K). The results only identify the papers and some secondary comparisons.\n\n- **The source paper:** A reference list cites Murday & Cotts as \"Self-diffusion coefficient of liquid lithium,\" J Chem Phys 48:4938–4945 (1968) (Murday JS, Cotts RM (1968) Self-diffusion coefficient of liquid lithium. J Chem Phys 48:4938–4945). I did not get the paper's text, so its numbers are unverified here.\n- **Secondary confirmation:** A 2012 molecular-dynamics study reports that its calculated self-diffusion coefficients are in good agreement with Murday's experiment results in atmosphere and fits an Arrhenius equation to its simulation results (We get the Arrhenius equation according to the simulation results.). That paper's abstract does not give the fitted numbers in the results I saw.\n- **Neutron scattering check:** A quasielastic neutron scattering study of liquid lithium at 500 and 830 K reports that the self-diffusion coefficient in liquid lithium obtained for both temperatures is in agreement with values in the literature. This is a useful cross-check near your temperature range.\n- **Caution on the solid-state value:** One result gives a fit with D0 = 0.038 cm²/s and Q ≈ 12 kcal/mol, but that is for solid lithium (the Messer & Noack NMR work), not liquid lithium, so it should not be used for 470 K. Note also that 470 K is just above lithium's melting point (about 454 K), so the liquid-phase data apply.\n- **Other experimental data:** Feinauer, Majer & Seeger (1994), \"Experimental data on 6Li and 7Li diffusivities,\" J Phys Condens Matter 6:L355, is cited alongside Murday & Cotts and may give additional liquid-phase values.\n\nTo get the actual D0 and activation energy, the next step is the full Murday & Cotts 1968 paper (J Chem Phys, 48, 4938) or the Wang & Ni 2012 article in *Heat and Mass Transfer*, which compares against it.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"cdf79a2a-b9ca-4d2e-afd7-856fe2f24685","uuid":"e705b4db-ba3d-4d0f-b36f-cef88a7e30b3","timestamp":"2026-11-01T07:38:04.546Z","tool_use_result":{"query":"liquid lithium self-diffusion \"cm2/s\" experimental 470 K 6.9e-5 OR \"D0\" activation ener